A double-slit interference experiment is used to determine the wavelength of light emitted from a laser, as shown in Fig. 5.2.
{{figure:9702_s16_21_q05_figure_5_2}}
The separation of the slits is $0.45\text{ mm}$. The fringes are viewed on a screen at a distance $D$ from the double slit.

The fringe width $x$ is measured for different distances $D$. The variation with $D$ of $x$ is shown in Fig. 5.3.
{{figure:9702_s16_21_q05_figure_5_3}}
